    {
      "id": "claim_f8d2779b446a499cba204edc0762679b",
      "statement": "In scripts/bootstrap-apps.sh, wait_for_nodes enforces Talos bootstrap ordering by skipping the wait when all nodes are already Ready=True, otherwise polling every 10 seconds until all nodes report Ready=False (Talos requires Ready=False before resources are applied), making the script safe to re-run on a running cluster. The subsequent apply_crds step (lines 87-118) is a cluster bootstrap step, not local tooling: it applies external-dns v0.23.0 and gateway-api v1.6.2 (experimental) CRDs server-side for bootstrap safety because Cilium, installed next by helmfile, has gatewayAPI enabled and needs the Gateway API CRDs before starting, even though Flux also manages those CRDs from Git.",
